%[text] %[text:anchor:T_361B34F4] # Fundamental Theorem of Calculus
%[text] [⇦ Main Menu](file:../../MainMenu.m)
%[text] One profound connection between differential and integral calculus is the relationship between [accumulation functions](file:./RiemannSoln.m) and [derivative functions](https://github.com/MathWorks-Teaching-Resources/Calculus-Derivatives). 
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![The area between a velocity as a function of time curve and the time axis tracks the positive and negative distances travelled by a skier from their starting location](text:image:45bc)
%[text] The geometric area under a curve corresponds to the total accumulation of the product of the values tracked along each axis. In this image velocity times time is distance. 
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"**Table of Contents**"}
%[text] 
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_51183E7B] **Before you get started:**
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_BF646A47] This live script is intended to be used with the code hidden. On the **View** tab of the MATLAB toolstrip, in the **View** section, select **Hide Code**.  Alternately, select **Hide Code** using the icon ![live script code hidden icon](text:image:2204) at the top right of the Live Editor pane.
%[text] ![Lightbulb mark](text:image:8953) Although the code is hidden, some interactivity requires familiarity with MATLAB. If you need more instruction, consider taking [MATLAB Onramp](https://matlabacademy.mathworks.com/details/matlab-onramp/gettingstarted), a free 2 hour online tutorial that teaches the essentials of MATLAB.
